---
import ServicePage from '../../components/services/ServicePage.astro';
import { SERVICES } from '../../data/site';

export const prerender = true;

const canonical = 'https://busqueneil.com/services/websites';
const svc = SERVICES[4];

const FAQ = [
  {
    q: 'How much does a custom website cost?',
    a: 'It depends on how many pages carry real work and whether you need copy written. A focused marketing site is the cheapest starting point; a site with a CMS, a blog and location pages costs more. You get a clear scope and price after the first conversation, before any work starts.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you use WordPress?',
    a: "I work in WordPress when a client already lives there and the team needs to edit without a developer. For new builds I usually reach for Astro, because it ships far less JavaScript, loads faster and doesn't need a monthly security-patch routine. I'll recommend whichever one fits how your team works.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Will my site rank on Google?',
    a: "A fast, well-structured site with real content is the floor, not the ceiling. I build clean technical SEO in from the start: proper headings, schema markup, fast Core Web Vitals and a real sitemap. Ranking beyond that depends on how competitive your market is and whether you keep publishing. I'll tell you which one you're in.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I edit it myself afterward?',
    a: "Yes, if you tell me up front, so I wire in a CMS your team can use. If nobody on your side wants to touch it, I skip the CMS, which makes the site faster and simpler, and you send me changes instead.",
  },
];
---
<ServicePage
  title="Custom Website Design and Development | Neil Busque"
  description="Fast, custom websites that look like your business instead of a template, and that search engines and AI assistants can actually read. Built by one person."
  canonical={canonical}
  heading="Custom websites that turn visitors into **booked calls**."
  lead="Fast, custom sites that feel like your business instead of a template, and that search engines and AI assistants can read. No page-builder bloat, no theme you have to fight."
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/' },
    { name: 'Services', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/services' },
    { name: 'Websites', url: canonical },
  ]}
  topic="websites"
  artSeed={svc.slug}
  artPalette="paper"
  summary={{ items: svc.items, facts: svc.facts }}
  related={['funnel-builder-kits', 'funnel-simulator']}
  relatedPalettes={['navy', 'paper']}
  faq={FAQ}
  service={{
    name: 'Website Design and Development',
    serviceType: ['Website design', 'Website development', 'Astro development', 'WordPress development', 'Technical SEO'],
    areaServed: ['New Jersey', 'New York', 'New York City', 'United States', 'Remote'],
  }}
>
  <h2>What is wrong with most small-business sites</h2>
  <p>Almost every site I get asked to fix has the same three problems, and none of them are about taste.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>It's slow.</strong> A theme plus a page builder plus fifteen plugins means a home page that takes six seconds on a phone. Most visitors are gone before the hero image loads.</li>
    <li><strong>It says nothing specific.</strong> "Quality service you can trust" is on ten thousand sites. It gives a visitor no reason to pick you, and gives Google nothing to rank.</li>
    <li><strong>Nobody can find anything.</strong> The thing you actually sell is three clicks deep, behind a menu built around your org chart instead of the visitor's question.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What I build instead</h2>
  <p>A site built around the few things a visitor is trying to do: understand what you sell, decide whether you're credible and take one obvious next step.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Custom design.</strong> Real typography and layout decisions, not a purchased theme with your logo dropped in.</li>
    <li><strong>Fast by construction.</strong> Astro ships almost no JavaScript by default, so the page is fast because of how it's built, not because a caching plugin patches over the problem.</li>
    <li><strong>Structured for search and AI.</strong> Clean headings, schema markup, a real sitemap, and pages that answer a question directly enough to be quoted by an AI assistant.</li>
    <li><strong>Connected.</strong> Forms and booking wired into your CRM, and an AI assistant that can answer questions and book calls if you want one.</li>
    <li><strong>Editable if you want it.</strong> A CMS when your team will use it, and no CMS when they won't.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Judge the work by this page</h2>
  <p>This site is mine, so you can judge the work by the page you're reading: how fast it loads, how it reads on your phone and whether the next step is obvious. Browse <a href="/work">the work</a> for the funnels, pages and apps behind it, or run your own site through the <a href="/analyzer">free landing page analyzer</a>.</p>

  <h2>How the build runs</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>A first conversation.</strong> What you sell, who buys it and what the site fails to do today.</li>
    <li><strong>Structure and copy first.</strong> Pages and words before pixels, because a beautiful layout wrapped around vague copy still doesn't convert.</li>
    <li><strong>Design and build.</strong> You see it live on a real link early and can change direction while it's cheap to change.</li>
    <li><strong>Launch.</strong> Domain, analytics, Search Console and sitemaps. Then it's yours.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What it costs to keep running</h2>
  <p>Usually very little. A static Astro site hosts free or nearly free on Vercel, there is no license to renew and there is no plugin subscription stack. That's the reason I build this way: the cheapest site to own is the one with the fewest moving parts.</p>
  <p>If one focused page is closer to what you need, read about <a href="/services/landing-pages">landing pages</a>. If the site has to carry leads all the way to a booked call, see <a href="/services/funnels">funnels</a>.</p>
</ServicePage>
